  "dom_id": "step-q87759",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178864/assets/56c2afca682997fa2ead3f4962d5de4e347d99164e257737f68ddafea385ae4f.png)\n\nWhat is a correct congruence statement for the quadrilaterals shown in the diagram above?",
  "worked_solution": "We have four pairs of congruent angles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠R & ≅∠F \\\\ ∠S & ≅∠E \\\\ ∠T & ≅∠H \\\\ ∠U & ≅∠G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have four pairs of congruent sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RS & =FE \\\\ ST & =EH \\\\ TU & =HG \\\\ UR & =GF.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince all corresponding sides and angles are congruent, the two quadrilaterals are congruent. In particular\n\n- vertex $R$ corresponds to vertex $F,$\n\n- vertex $S$ corresponds to vertex $E,$\n\n- vertex $T$ corresponds to vertex $H,$ and\n\n- vertex $U$ corresponds to vertex $G.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that a correct congruence statement is\n\n$$\nRSTU≅FEHG.\n$$",
